00:15:07,282 --> 00:15:09,326
- [Walter] Please, Dr. Lind.
- What the f...

239
00:15:09,993 --> 00:15:14,122
Guys like you and me,
we don't do normal hours, do we?

240
00:15:16,625 --> 00:15:19,878
I've been fixated on Hollow Earth
for as long as you have.

241
00:15:19,961 --> 00:15:24,216
Your theory that it's the birthplace
of all Titans is fascinating.

242
00:15:24,341 --> 00:15:26,551
Your book was very impressive.

243
00:15:26,635 --> 00:15:29,429
Oh, yeah?
Well, I got about 30 unsold boxes

244
00:15:29,513 --> 00:15:30,972
in my apartment if you want some.

245
00:15:31,056 --> 00:15:32,224
[chuckles]

246
00:15:32,307 --> 00:15:33,475
Walt Simmons.

247
00:15:34,392 --> 00:15:36,186
I know who you are, sir. It's an honor.

248
00:15:36,311 --> 00:15:39,898
No, the honor is mine.
As is the urgency.

249
00:15:39,981 --> 00:15:43,235
Godzilla has never attacked us
unprovoked before.

250
00:15:43,318 --> 00:15:45,570
These are dangerous times, Dr. Lind.

251
00:15:46,238 --> 00:15:47,447
Allow me to introduce

252
00:15:47,531 --> 00:15:50,784
our Apex chief technology officer,
Mr. Ren Serizawa.

253
00:15:51,576 --> 00:15:54,746
He has an interesting thing to show you.

254
00:15:57,457 --> 00:15:58,458
[beeps]

255
00:15:59,167 --> 00:16:02,504
Magnetic imaging
from one of our new satellites.

256
00:16:03,130 --> 00:16:05,132
You know what this is, right?

257
00:16:05,715 --> 00:16:07,134
[Nathan] Hollow Earth.

258
00:16:07,217 --> 00:16:10,428
[Walter] An ecosystem
as vast as any ocean,

259
00:16:10,512 --> 00:16:11,847
right beneath our feet.

260
00:16:16,101 --> 00:16:18,478
This energy signal is enormous.

261
00:16:18,562 --> 00:16:21,982
And almost identical
to readings from <i>Gojira.</i>

262
00:16:22,065 --> 00:16:24,317
[Walter] As our sun
fuels the planet's surface,

263
00:16:24,401 --> 00:16:26,778
this energy sustains the Hollow Earth,

264
00:16:26,862 --> 00:16:31,158
enabling life as powerful
as our aggressive Titan friend.

265
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:34,536
If we can harness this life force,

266
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:37,497
we'll have a weapon
that can compete with Godzilla.

267
00:16:38,206 --> 00:16:40,333
I need your help to find it.

268
00:16:40,417 --> 00:16:42,085
[chuckling]

269
00:16:42,919 --> 00:16:45,922
I don't know if I'm the right guy
for the job.

270
00:16:47,090 --> 00:16:48,091
Did you read the reviews?

271
00:16:48,175 --> 00:16:51,344
"A sci-fi quack
trading in fringe physics."

272
00:16:51,595 --> 00:16:53,221
Look where they put my office.

273
00:16:53,305 --> 00:16:55,640
I'm in the basement
right across from flute class.

274
00:16:56,725 --> 00:16:59,060
Besides, I'm not with Monarch anymore.

275
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:01,605
And Hollow Earth entry is impossible.

276
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:03,648
We tried.

277
00:17:06,568 --> 00:17:08,695
I'm sorry about your brother.

278
00:17:09,613 --> 00:17:11,531
He was a true pioneer.

279
00:17:11,865 --> 00:17:12,866
Thanks.

280
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:15,869
[sniffles, clears throat]

281
00:17:17,621 --> 00:17:19,998
See, all of our forward scans

282
00:17:20,081 --> 00:17:23,376
suggest a habitable environment
down there.

283
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:28,798
So, what really went wrong
on your brother's mission?

284
00:17:31,676 --> 00:17:33,720
When they tried to enter,

285
00:17:34,596 --> 00:17:36,848
they hit a gravitational inversion.

286
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:41,645
A whole planet's worth of gravity
reversed in a split second.

287
00:17:43,688 --> 00:17:46,399
They were crushed in an instant.

288
00:17:48,485 --> 00:17:51,905
What if I told you that we, at Apex,

289
00:17:51,988 --> 00:17:56,618
have created a phenomenal craft
which could sustain such an inversion?

290
00:17:59,537 --> 00:18:01,873
The Hollow Earth Aerial Vehicle.

291
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,667
HEAV.

292
00:18:06,878 --> 00:18:10,382
We can make the journey
to Hollow Earth possible, Dr. Lind.

293
00:18:10,465 --> 00:18:12,759
But we need you to lead the mission.

294
00:18:19,474 --> 00:18:20,600
Help me.

295
00:18:22,394 --> 00:18:23,895
Help everyone.

296
00:18:24,896 --> 00:18:29,567
Finding this needle in a haystack
is our best shot against Godzilla.

297
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:33,280
Well, I, uh, might have an idea.

298
00:18:34,155 --> 00:18:35,198
But it's crazy.

299
00:18:35,365 --> 00:18:38,952
I love crazy ideas. They made me rich.

300
00:18:40,745 --> 00:18:42,914
[Nathan] Are you guys familiar
with genetic memory?

301
00:18:43,373 --> 00:18:46,084
It's a theory that all Titans
share a common impulse

302
00:18:46,167 --> 00:18:47,585
to return to their evolutionary source.

303
00:18:48,169 --> 00:18:49,546
Like spawning salmon.

304
00:18:49,713 --> 00:18:53,550
Exactly. Or a... Or a homing pigeon.

305
00:18:53,925 --> 00:18:56,052
So if this is the Titans' home

306
00:18:56,219 --> 00:18:58,305
and this life force sustains them...

307
00:18:58,471 --> 00:19:00,098
A Titan could show you the way.

308
00:19:01,850 --> 00:19:02,892
[Nathan] Yeah.

309
00:19:04,185 --> 00:19:05,854
With a little help of an old colleague.

310
00:19:13,528 --> 00:19:14,863
[grunts softly]

311
00:19:40,055 --> 00:19:41,139
[Ilene] Ugh, where is it?

312
00:19:41,222 --> 00:19:42,223
[receptionist] <i>Dr. Andrews,</i>

313
00:19:42,307 --> 00:19:44,726
<i>you have a visitor
waiting for you at security.</i>

314
00:19:47,604 --> 00:19:48,605
[in sign language]

315
00:19:51,608 --> 00:19:52,650
[sighs] Okay.

316
00:20:03,286 --> 00:20:04,496
[chuckles softly]

317
00:20:06,289 --> 00:20:07,582
[thunder rumbles]

318
00:20:07,665 --> 00:20:09,751
[Ilene] A power source in Hollow Earth?

319
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:12,003
This sounds nuts, Nathan, even for you.

320
00:20:12,170 --> 00:20:14,964
[Nathan] It's there!
We just need Kong to bring us to it!

321
00:20:15,131 --> 00:20:17,550
[Ilene] The second you take Kong
out of containment,

322
00:20:17,634 --> 00:20:18,843
Godzilla's gonna come for him.

323
00:20:18,927 --> 00:20:20,720
[Nathan] You said you can't
keep him here forever.

324
00:20:20,804 --> 00:20:23,807
No. Our meddling has already
wreaked havoc on Kong's habitat.

325
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:25,475
No way am I letting you drag him

326
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:27,185
halfway across the world
to use him as a weapon.

327
00:20:27,268 --> 00:20:29,604
[Nathan] No, not as a weapon.
As an ally.

328
00:20:29,687 --> 00:20:31,731
To protect us, lead the way down there.

329
00:20:31,898 --> 00:20:34,025
What even makes you think
that he'll go in?

330
00:20:34,192 --> 00:20:35,902
You always believed that Skull Island

331
00:20:35,985 --> 00:20:38,363
was like Hollow Earth
come to the surface, right?

332
00:20:38,446 --> 00:20:40,031
And that's where Kong's ancestors
came from.

333
00:20:40,115 --> 00:20:41,116
Mm-hmm.

334
00:20:41,199 --> 00:20:44,202
Through the entrance in Antarctica,
we could help him find a new home.

335
00:20:44,702 --> 00:20:46,454
And he could save ours.

336
00:20:47,414 --> 00:20:48,415
Hers.

337
00:20:48,998 --> 00:20:51,418
That power source may be our only hope.

338
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:54,295
We gotta stop Godzilla.
This is our only chance.

339
00:20:55,255 --> 00:20:56,714
We have to take it.

340
00:20:58,550 --> 00:20:59,968
[creatures chittering]

341
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:04,472
[electrical crackling and humming]

342
00:21:06,057 --> 00:21:07,225
[sighs]

343
00:21:14,274 --> 00:21:15,567
- Okay.
- Yes!

344
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:18,736
But when it comes to Kong,
what I say goes.

345
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:20,864
You name the terms. Thank you.

346
00:21:22,615 --> 00:21:24,826
Sorry. Thank you.

347
00:21:26,161 --> 00:21:27,162
You won't regret this.

348
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,747
- Mm, I already regret this.
- [thudding]

349
00:21:31,583 --> 00:21:33,376
- [sighs]
- [in sign language]

350
00:21:43,011 --> 00:21:44,137
[Ilene sighs]

351
00:21:49,726 --> 00:21:51,436
[exhales heavily] Come on.

352
00:21:55,064 --> 00:21:57,192
[country song playing]

353
00:22:04,407 --> 00:22:07,494
<i>If you could see me now</i>

354
00:22:08,995 --> 00:22:13,333
<i>The one who said that he'd rather roam</i>

355
00:22:13,416 --> 00:22:15,418
[breathing heavily]

356
00:22:15,668 --> 00:22:21,132
<i>The one who said he'd rather be alone</i>

357
00:22:22,133 --> 00:22:26,721
<i>If you could only see me now</i>

358
00:22:27,472 --> 00:22:30,934
<i>I've been too long in the wind</i>

359
00:22:31,601 --> 00:22:34,062
<i>Too long in the rain</i>

360
00:22:34,145 --> 00:22:35,855
[indistinct radio chatter]

361
00:22:35,939 --> 00:22:39,359
<i>Taking any comfort that I can</i>

362
00:22:41,277 --> 00:22:44,364
<i>Looking back and longing for</i>

363
00:22:44,447 --> 00:22:46,783
<i>The freedom of my chains...</i>

364
00:22:46,866 --> 00:22:48,409
[door thuds, buzzer sounds]

365
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:52,080
Whoo! Jeez,
I can smell him from up here.

366
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:54,582
Well, he can smell you, too.

367
00:22:54,707 --> 00:22:56,709
[Kong moaning]

368
00:23:02,882 --> 00:23:04,467
Still not a fan, huh?

369
00:23:08,137 --> 00:23:09,264
[in sign language]

370
00:23:10,431 --> 00:23:11,432
What's she saying?

371
00:23:12,642 --> 00:23:14,269
Just an Iwi expression.

372
00:23:14,352 --> 00:23:15,770
It means that you're very brave.

373
00:23:15,937 --> 00:23:16,938
- Yeah?
- [Ilene] Mm-hmm.

374
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:21,526
[Nathan] Hey, use a light touch
on the sedatives.

375
00:23:21,609 --> 00:23:22,986
He's our escort.

376
00:23:23,069 --> 00:23:25,530
We can't have him comatose
when we reach Hollow Earth.

377
00:23:25,613 --> 00:23:27,615
What if Kong doesn't go willingly?

378
00:23:27,699 --> 00:23:29,450
- What do you do then?
- [PA chimes]

379
00:23:29,534 --> 00:23:32,829
[woman on PA] <i>Dr. Lind, please report
to the forward deck. Dr. Lind.</i>

380
00:23:32,996 --> 00:23:33,997
Excuse me.

381
00:23:35,707 --> 00:23:37,917
- New arrivals.
- [in sign language]

382
00:23:42,589 --> 00:23:44,757
- [metal creaks]
- [Kong grunting]

383
00:23:55,810 --> 00:23:57,353
[growls softly]

384
00:24:00,231 --> 00:24:01,232
Welcome.

385
00:24:04,110 --> 00:24:08,114
Wow. Who's the idiot
who came up with this idea?

386
00:24:09,073 --> 00:24:10,742
- Ha-ha.
- I'm Maia Simmons.

387
00:24:10,825 --> 00:24:11,868
My father sent me.

388
00:24:11,993 --> 00:24:13,453
I run point for Apex.

389
00:24:13,536 --> 00:24:15,204
Nathan Lind, mission chief.

390
00:24:15,288 --> 00:24:16,664
[Kong growls]

391
00:24:17,832 --> 00:24:20,293
Yeah, don't worry.
I'm just here to babysit.

392
00:24:20,877 --> 00:24:22,253
- [Kong growls]
- [metal clangs]

393
00:24:22,337 --> 00:24:26,132
The Hollow Earth Aerial Vehicles are
on their way to Antarctica as we speak.

394
00:24:26,299 --> 00:24:28,593
I know you people
think you're cutting-edge,

395
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:30,261
but these prototypes we're loaning you

396
00:24:30,345 --> 00:24:33,723
will make what you've been flying
look like used Miatas.

397
00:24:33,890 --> 00:24:35,016
I love Miatas.

398
00:24:35,183 --> 00:24:37,644
Forget about the price tag,
which is obscene, of course.

399
00:24:37,769 --> 00:24:39,562
The antigravity engines alone produce

400
00:24:39,646 --> 00:24:41,773
enough charge
to light up Vegas for a week.

401
00:24:43,232 --> 00:24:44,984
Feel free to be impressed.

402
00:24:45,985 --> 00:24:47,070
Wow.

403
00:24:47,945 --> 00:24:49,322
[thunder crashes]

404
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:52,241
[moaning]

405
00:25:00,083 --> 00:25:02,919
[Nathan] All right, we'll be
at the Antarctica entry in 48 hours.

406
00:25:03,461 --> 00:25:05,838
This path will get us into Hollow Earth.

407
00:25:06,798 --> 00:25:10,301
Once we're inside,
Kong should lead us to the power source.

408
00:25:10,385 --> 00:25:13,388
Now, the gravitational inversion
will be quite intense.

409
00:25:13,471 --> 00:25:16,933
Our best guess is that on entry,
it'll feel like bungee jumping...

410
00:25:17,016 --> 00:25:19,185
with the cord tied
to your lower intestine.

411
00:25:19,352 --> 00:25:21,354
But if your helicopters
are as good as you say...

412
00:25:21,521 --> 00:25:22,605
HEAVs.

413
00:25:22,772 --> 00:25:25,108
If your HEAVs are as good
as you say they are,

414
00:25:25,525 --> 00:25:27,026
I believe we can do this.

415
00:25:27,193 --> 00:25:28,569
[Maia] They'll do the job.

416
00:25:29,445 --> 00:25:31,030
You just gotta do yours.

417
00:25:31,531 --> 00:25:32,782
Excellent.

418
00:25:35,201 --> 00:25:36,202
[Wilcox] Dr. Andrews.

419
00:25:37,245 --> 00:25:39,914
We've avoided all of Godzilla's
known territorial waters

420
00:25:39,997 --> 00:25:41,249
according to your guidelines.

421
00:25:41,666 --> 00:25:42,667
Good.

422
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:43,876
Do I need to be concerned?

423
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:46,045
Yes. They do have a way
of sensing threats.

424
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:48,506
And we believe that they had
an ancient rivalry.

425
00:25:48,673 --> 00:25:51,467
The myths say that their ancestors
fought each other in a great war.

426
00:25:51,634 --> 00:25:54,804
So if they meet again,
who bows to who, is that it?

427
00:25:54,887 --> 00:25:55,888
[scoffs]

428
00:25:55,972 --> 00:25:58,307
No, I spent ten years
on that island studying him.

429
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:00,935
I know this for sure.

430
00:26:01,310 --> 00:26:03,438
Kong bows to no one.

431
00:26:13,990 --> 00:26:15,825
[faint, muffled moaning]

432
00:26:18,327 --> 00:26:20,329
[muffled pulsing]

433
00:26:31,841 --> 00:26:33,468
[pulsing quickening]

434
00:26:38,931 --> 00:26:40,308
[rain pattering]

435
00:26:42,560 --> 00:26:43,936
[loud thud]

436
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:53,571
Is she supposed to be out there?

437
00:26:53,654 --> 00:26:55,656
- [thudding continues]
- [metallic whining]

438
00:27:04,540 --> 00:27:05,750
[roars]

439
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:17,678
[faint, muffled roaring]

440
00:27:20,223 --> 00:27:21,641
[faint, muffled grunting]

441
00:27:43,538 --> 00:27:44,789
[Kong grunts softly]

442
00:27:53,214 --> 00:27:55,007
[Kong moaning]

443
00:27:58,845 --> 00:28:00,346
Jia, come on. Come on.

444
00:28:03,099 --> 00:28:04,433
[in sign language]

445
00:28:09,605 --> 00:28:10,648
[huffs]

446
00:28:19,699 --> 00:28:21,242
[moaning]

447
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:37,300
[grunting softly]

448
00:28:49,729 --> 00:28:51,147
[groaning]

449
00:28:55,902 --> 00:28:57,945
Did the monkey just talk?

450
00:29:03,159 --> 00:29:04,827
[Bernie on speaker]
<i>Okay, class, listen up.</i>

451
00:29:05,494 --> 00:29:09,040
<i>In the midst of Godzilla's attack
on Apex Pensacola,</i>

452
00:29:09,206 --> 00:29:12,460
<i>I found some crazy tech
with no official classification.</i>

453
00:29:13,628 --> 00:29:14,629
<i>What I saw doesn't match</i>

454
00:29:14,712 --> 00:29:16,505
<i>any of the engineering specs
I've ever seen.</i>

455
00:29:16,672 --> 00:29:19,800
<i>So what are they working on
in such blackout secrecy, hmm?</i>

456
00:29:20,551 --> 00:29:22,094
<i>This could be the thread
that finally unravels</i>

457
00:29:22,178 --> 00:29:23,846
<i>the Apex sweater of conspiracy.</i>

458
00:29:23,930 --> 00:29:25,681
<i>You better believe
I'm gonna keep tugging.</i>

459
00:29:26,599 --> 00:29:27,850
<i>For now, I'm secure.</i>

460
00:29:27,934 --> 00:29:30,728
<i>Anonymous and hiding in plain sight
as I continue my mission.</i>

461
00:29:31,479 --> 00:29:34,065
["Breaking The Law"
blaring on van speaker]

462
00:29:34,148 --> 00:29:36,275
<i>Breaking the law
Breaking the law</i>

463
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:39,904
<i>Breaking the law
Breaking the law</i>

464
00:29:42,031 --> 00:29:43,532
[music stops]

465
00:29:46,452 --> 00:29:48,788
To be clear, my brother
can never know we took his van.

466
00:29:48,871 --> 00:29:51,123
Josh, to be clear,
even if we got into an accident,

467
00:29:51,207 --> 00:29:52,208
I don't think he could tell.

468
00:29:52,291 --> 00:29:54,502
No, no, my brother would never
let you drive either.

469
00:29:54,585 --> 00:29:55,670
My mission, my wheel.

470
00:29:55,753 --> 00:29:57,046
I just don't think it's a good idea,

471
00:29:57,129 --> 00:29:59,173
looking for some secret weirdo
off the Internet.

472
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:01,550
I mean, we just had
an assembly about this.

473
00:30:01,634 --> 00:30:04,011
He's not a weirdo.
He's a covert investigator.

474
00:30:04,095 --> 00:30:05,888
And he's the only one
looking for the truth

475
00:30:05,972 --> 00:30:07,473
about Godzilla and Apex.

476
00:30:07,556 --> 00:30:10,142
So let him look.
Why do we have to help him?

477
00:30:10,226 --> 00:30:11,394
[sighs] Because...

478
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:13,562
If we don't, nobody else will.

479
00:30:15,272 --> 00:30:16,649
Are you coming or not?

480
00:30:17,441 --> 00:30:18,859
Obviously I'm coming.

481
00:30:18,943 --> 00:30:20,361
[van door rattles]

482
00:30:20,444 --> 00:30:21,821
It's stuck.

483
00:30:21,904 --> 00:30:24,073
- [engine revs]
- Wait, wait, wait, wait!

484
00:30:34,625 --> 00:30:36,460
[Bernie on speaker] <i>Mind control.
Read up on it, sheep.</i>

485
00:30:36,544 --> 00:30:38,212
<i>Psionic link technology is a reality.</i>

486
00:30:38,295 --> 00:30:40,339
<i>That's right.
One brain controlling another.</i>

487
00:30:40,423 --> 00:30:41,424
Oh, man.

488
00:30:41,507 --> 00:30:44,135
[Bernie] <i>Imagine that on a global scale
and Apex is invincible.</i>

489
00:30:44,218 --> 00:30:46,095
We've been listening
to this weirdo for hours.

490
00:30:46,178 --> 00:30:47,888
- [Madison] Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- [tires screech]

491
00:30:47,972 --> 00:30:49,682
Whoa! Knock it off!

492
00:30:50,266 --> 00:30:52,143
Wait, this is the part
I was telling you about.

493
00:30:52,226 --> 00:30:54,145
[Bernie] <i>...need special UV
to even know you've been marked!</i>

494
00:30:54,228 --> 00:30:55,730
<i>One or two gallons won't cut it.</i>

495
00:30:55,813 --> 00:30:58,190
<i>I need my bleach in bulk!</i>

496
00:30:58,691 --> 00:31:00,776
<i>Because spy dust is real, people!</i>

497
00:31:00,860 --> 00:31:02,403
<i>I mean, come on,
invisible to the naked eye...</i>

498
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:04,030
- [turns off stereo]
- That's how we find him.

499
00:31:04,113 --> 00:31:05,865
- The bleach.
- Bleach?

500
00:31:06,157 --> 00:31:07,992
He consumes a ton of bleach.

501
00:31:08,075 --> 00:31:09,410
He drinks bleach?

502
00:31:10,578 --> 00:31:12,038
Showers with it.

503
00:31:12,121 --> 00:31:14,915
Oh! Yeah, I shower with bleach.
No, what?

504
00:31:15,082 --> 00:31:17,668
Prevention against
organic tracking technology.

505
00:31:17,835 --> 00:31:19,795
See? Tradecraft.

506
00:31:20,504 --> 00:31:22,840
Would've made more sense
if he just drank it.

507
00:31:28,763 --> 00:31:30,473
[Madison] Come on, just one more place.

508
00:31:30,639 --> 00:31:32,725
Madison, this is getting old.

509
00:31:33,225 --> 00:31:34,560
Hey, you sell bleach?

510
00:31:35,770 --> 00:31:37,855
Is this another one of those
Internet challenge things?

511
00:31:37,938 --> 00:31:39,565
When I sold those kids
those detergent pods,

512
00:31:39,648 --> 00:31:41,317
I didn't know they were gonna eat them.

513
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:43,527
I'm still dealing
with the lawsuits from that.

514
00:31:43,694 --> 00:31:46,530
Look, we're looking for a guy
who works for Apex Cybernetics.

515
00:31:46,697 --> 00:31:49,366
Buys a lot of bleach. Like every night.

516
00:31:49,533 --> 00:31:53,329
He's probably paranoid,
high-strung, doesn't like daylight.

517
00:31:53,537 --> 00:31:56,373
You know, has a lot of crumbs
in his beard, if he has a beard.

518
00:31:56,457 --> 00:31:59,668
Okay, look, you kids want some candy?
Because I can help you with candy.

519
00:32:00,086 --> 00:32:03,214
Look at me in the eye. Okay?
I need information.

520
00:32:03,339 --> 00:32:04,590
Yeah, we want lots of candy.

521
00:32:06,634 --> 00:32:08,010
What are you doing?
You think...?

522
00:32:08,177 --> 00:32:11,305
Oh, you mean Bernie.

523
00:32:12,223 --> 00:32:13,516
Yeah, I know that guy.

524
00:32:13,599 --> 00:32:15,059
He buys, like, a ton of bleach.

525
00:32:15,226 --> 00:32:16,519
I know where he is, too.

526
00:32:16,602 --> 00:32:18,729
If you buy a live fish,
I'll give you his address.

527
00:32:19,438 --> 00:32:20,773
[banging on door]

528
00:32:21,982 --> 00:32:23,109
[Madison] Bernie?

529
00:32:23,818 --> 00:32:25,236
[Bernie] Mister...
[clears throat] Mis...

530
00:32:25,319 --> 00:32:26,320
- [thud]
- [Bernie groans]

531
00:32:26,403 --> 00:32:27,571
[in deep voice] Mister Bernie not home.

532
00:32:27,655 --> 00:32:30,783
- Yep, that was definitely Mister Bernie.
- Yeah. Um...

533
00:32:30,866 --> 00:32:35,162
Hi! Hi. Listen, we wanna talk
about Apex and Godzilla.

534
00:32:35,329 --> 00:32:37,498
[Bernie] No. No. No.

535
00:32:37,581 --> 00:32:40,876
I... I got your faces.
I contact authorities. Yes.

536
00:32:41,293 --> 00:32:42,378
[Josh] For knocking on a door?

537
00:32:42,461 --> 00:32:43,754
[Bernie chuckles] No. No.

538
00:32:43,921 --> 00:32:47,967
Bernie, you don't trust the authorities.
My name is Madison Russell.

539
00:32:48,134 --> 00:32:50,845
My father works for Monarch
and my mother was...

540
00:32:51,011 --> 00:32:53,013
Emma Russell, right?

541
00:32:54,974 --> 00:32:57,726
Before we go any farther,
I got one question.

542
00:32:58,686 --> 00:32:59,937
Tap or no tap?

543
00:33:00,229 --> 00:33:01,480
No tap.

544
00:33:01,981 --> 00:33:04,275
- Excuse me, what is "tap"?
- Water.

545
00:33:04,441 --> 00:33:06,694
They put fluoride in it.
Learned it from the Nazis.

546
00:33:06,777 --> 00:33:09,280
Theory is it makes you docile,
easy to manipulate.

547
00:33:09,446 --> 00:33:10,906
Oh, I drink tap water.

548
00:33:12,032 --> 00:33:13,450
Yeah, I kind of figured that.

549
00:33:13,576 --> 00:33:15,035
But she does the thinking
for both of you,

550
00:33:15,119 --> 00:33:16,620
so it should be all right.

551
00:33:17,079 --> 00:33:18,455
- Thanks.
- Okay.

552
00:33:18,956 --> 00:33:19,957
What you got?

553
00:33:21,667 --> 00:33:24,503
I believe Godzilla's most recent attacks
haven't just been random.

554
00:33:24,670 --> 00:33:26,714
I think he targeted the Apex facility.

555
00:33:26,881 --> 00:33:28,257
I'm of the same opinion.

556
00:33:28,424 --> 00:33:30,801
But why?
What is Apex up to that's provoking him?

557
00:33:30,968 --> 00:33:33,387
For five years, I embedded
myself inside this company,

558
00:33:33,554 --> 00:33:35,431
trying to figure out
what their game was.

559
00:33:35,598 --> 00:33:37,558
Then, last week...

560
00:33:38,142 --> 00:33:39,143
I saw this.

561
00:33:40,728 --> 00:33:43,772
A manifest of huge cargo
being sent from here

562
00:33:43,856 --> 00:33:45,149
to Apex headquarters in Hong Kong,

563
00:33:45,232 --> 00:33:48,527
which makes no sense because
we are not equipped for heavy shipping.

564
00:33:48,694 --> 00:33:49,862
- Then what?
- And then boom!

565
00:33:50,029 --> 00:33:51,655
Godzilla shows up.

566
00:33:51,739 --> 00:33:52,865
Caved in half the facility,

567
00:33:52,990 --> 00:33:54,992
but I got a sneak peek
at some suspicious tech

568
00:33:55,117 --> 00:33:56,827
which was hidden in a secret bunker.

569
00:33:56,911 --> 00:33:58,662
I mean,
some pretty damn suspicious tech.

570
00:33:58,829 --> 00:34:00,873
Yeah, but what is that?

571
00:34:04,919 --> 00:34:06,212
That's, um...

572
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:10,132
That's Katzunari single malt whiskey.

573
00:34:10,299 --> 00:34:12,259
Yeah, but it's in a gun holster.

574
00:34:12,635 --> 00:34:14,511
It was a gift from my Sara.

575
00:34:14,678 --> 00:34:15,679
You have a Sara?

576
00:34:15,846 --> 00:34:16,931
She was my wife.

577
00:34:17,473 --> 00:34:19,433
Um, she passed on.

578
00:34:21,936 --> 00:34:23,062
[Bernie sighs]

579
00:34:23,145 --> 00:34:24,647
She was my rock.

580
00:34:25,189 --> 00:34:26,523
My truth.

581
00:34:27,441 --> 00:34:30,444
I'll tell you something,
the day that this goes empty,

582
00:34:30,527 --> 00:34:32,238
that's the day you know I've given up.

583
00:34:37,576 --> 00:34:38,702
[Madison] Bernie.

584
00:34:39,370 --> 00:34:40,955
I think we can help each other.

585
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:47,503
Okay, I guess now that we're a team,

586
00:34:47,586 --> 00:34:49,672
I feel like we should
come up with a plan.

587
00:34:49,964 --> 00:34:51,257
We're breaking into Apex.

588
00:34:51,423 --> 00:34:53,259
- [Josh] Wait, what?
- [Bernie] You heard her.

589
00:34:53,509 --> 00:34:54,969
Tap water.

590
00:34:55,261 --> 00:34:56,637
Shit.

591
00:35:02,726 --> 00:35:03,894
[groans]

592
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:13,112
[grunts contentedly]

593
00:35:26,583 --> 00:35:27,710
[Ilene] Hey.

594
00:35:31,630 --> 00:35:32,798
[in sign language]

595
00:36:08,751 --> 00:36:10,085
Thank you.

596
00:36:11,754 --> 00:36:13,047
How is she?

597
00:36:13,422 --> 00:36:16,342
Calm. So calm, it's scary. [chuckles]

598
00:36:16,425 --> 00:36:18,594
That was extraordinary.

599
00:36:18,761 --> 00:36:22,431
I have been signing the alphabet.
Basic commands.

600
00:36:22,598 --> 00:36:25,059
I thought that he showed recognition,
but he never...

601
00:36:25,225 --> 00:36:27,811
Do you have any idea how long
they've been communicating?

602
00:36:27,978 --> 00:36:29,063
No.

603
00:36:29,480 --> 00:36:31,440
I knew that they had a bond.

604
00:36:31,607 --> 00:36:33,233
He trusts her.

605
00:36:33,317 --> 00:36:35,235
Without her,
he'd be tearing the ship apart.

606
00:36:37,112 --> 00:36:40,240
You know, Jia's parents
were killed on the island.

607
00:36:40,407 --> 00:36:44,161
When the storm took over the island,
it wiped out the native people.

608
00:36:44,328 --> 00:36:45,662
But Kong saved her.

609
00:36:45,829 --> 00:36:47,790
She had nowhere to go.

610
00:36:47,956 --> 00:36:51,627
So I made a promise,
then and there, to protect her.

611
00:36:52,127 --> 00:36:56,048
And I think that in some way,
he did the same.

612
00:36:59,051 --> 00:37:01,261
Do you think he would take
directions from her?

613
00:37:03,597 --> 00:37:04,598
No.

614
00:37:04,765 --> 00:37:06,767
If we have someone
who can keep the reins on Kong...

615
00:37:06,934 --> 00:37:08,894
Yeah, no one can keep the reins on Kong.

616
00:37:10,396 --> 00:37:11,939
And she's a child.

617
00:37:24,201 --> 00:37:26,203
[distant, muffled pulsing]

618
00:37:33,836 --> 00:37:35,838
[muffled groaning]

619
00:37:40,217 --> 00:37:42,928
[Nathan] I know Jia is only a child.

620
00:37:43,679 --> 00:37:46,140
But she's the only one
he'll communicate with.

621
00:37:47,683 --> 00:37:50,436
<i>And we need Kong
to find that power source.</i>

622
00:37:52,187 --> 00:37:54,022
The world needs him.

623
00:37:56,066 --> 00:37:57,860
[alarm blaring]

624
00:37:57,943 --> 00:37:59,445
[muffled moaning]

625
00:38:03,699 --> 00:38:05,117
[indistinct shouting]

626
00:38:07,244 --> 00:38:08,620
What's she saying?

627
00:38:08,954 --> 00:38:09,955
Godzilla.

628
00:38:10,164 --> 00:38:12,458
[roaring]

629
00:38:14,001 --> 00:38:16,003
[urgent chatter]

630
00:38:17,588 --> 00:38:19,673
- [Kong grunts]
- [metal clangs]

631
00:38:19,756 --> 00:38:20,924
Did we change course?

632
00:38:21,091 --> 00:38:23,010
No. We're nowhere
near the areas you flagged.

633
00:38:23,177 --> 00:38:24,928
It looks like he's coming for us anyway.

634
00:38:25,095 --> 00:38:26,138
[Ilene] He's not coming for us.

635
00:38:26,305 --> 00:38:28,724
Him? Then dump him. Dump the monkey!

636
00:38:28,891 --> 00:38:30,893
How about we throw you off instead, huh?

637
00:38:30,976 --> 00:38:32,769
[roars]

638
00:38:32,936 --> 00:38:34,104
We have to release him.

639
00:38:34,271 --> 00:38:35,731
If we lose Kong, the mission is over.

640
00:38:35,814 --> 00:38:36,940
He's a sitting duck out there.

641
00:38:37,107 --> 00:38:39,067
We have to let him protect himself.
And us.

642
00:38:39,151 --> 00:38:40,861
[weapons firing]

643
00:38:41,862 --> 00:38:42,863
[roars]

644
00:39:07,012 --> 00:39:09,014
[roaring]

645
00:39:17,272 --> 00:39:18,273
[groans]

646
00:39:18,357 --> 00:39:19,191
Delta...

647
00:39:19,274 --> 00:39:20,275
[screams]

648
00:39:40,796 --> 00:39:42,256
[roaring]

649
00:39:50,013 --> 00:39:51,098
[high-pitched roar]

650
00:39:51,723 --> 00:39:53,100
[roaring]

651
00:40:08,532 --> 00:40:09,950
[roars]

652
00:40:11,118 --> 00:40:12,327
[men scream]

653
00:40:14,454 --> 00:40:16,456
[people screaming]

654
00:40:23,964 --> 00:40:25,048
[growls]

655
00:40:30,053 --> 00:40:31,388
[Godzilla groans]

656
00:40:33,223 --> 00:40:34,850
[Ilene] Oh, my God, Jia!

657
00:40:35,017 --> 00:40:36,059
Nathan?

658
00:41:03,920 --> 00:41:05,005
[roars]

659
00:41:05,088 --> 00:41:06,423
[yelling]

660
00:41:19,436 --> 00:41:21,146
[both snarling]

661
00:41:37,204 --> 00:41:38,914
[alarm beeping]

662
00:41:49,383 --> 00:41:50,801
[growling]

663
00:41:53,345 --> 00:41:55,180
[roaring]

664
00:42:00,143 --> 00:42:01,269
[moans]

665
00:42:07,401 --> 00:42:08,527
[roars]

666
00:42:39,182 --> 00:42:40,767
[roaring]

667
00:42:50,152 --> 00:42:51,153
[roars]

668
00:43:12,132 --> 00:43:13,675
[Godzilla screeching]

669
00:43:20,682 --> 00:43:22,100
[screeches]

670
00:43:25,687 --> 00:43:27,063
[Kong moans]

671
00:43:37,282 --> 00:43:38,909
[electrical throbbing]

672
00:44:02,516 --> 00:44:03,725
[Godzilla screeches]

673
00:44:28,416 --> 00:44:29,584
He needs our help.

674
00:44:29,668 --> 00:44:31,545
There must be some way
to disorient Godzilla.

675
00:44:31,878 --> 00:44:32,921
Depth charges.

676
00:44:33,588 --> 00:44:35,048
[buzzer sounding]

677
00:44:46,142 --> 00:44:47,769
[snarling]

678
00:44:54,359 --> 00:44:56,528
[growls, yells]

679
00:44:57,529 --> 00:44:58,905
[muffled explosion]

680
00:45:18,884 --> 00:45:19,801
[man] Run!

681
00:45:24,097 --> 00:45:25,223
[retches]

682
00:45:27,434 --> 00:45:28,894
[coughing]

683
00:45:44,534 --> 00:45:45,994
[Nathan] He's circling back.

684
00:45:46,161 --> 00:45:48,580
This won't end
until one of them submits.

685
00:45:49,164 --> 00:45:50,916
[groaning softly]

686
00:45:51,708 --> 00:45:53,418
- [Nathan] Shut it down.
- What?

687
00:45:54,127 --> 00:45:55,337
All of it.

688
00:45:55,503 --> 00:45:56,963
Guns, engines.

689
00:45:57,505 --> 00:46:00,216
- Shut it down. Right now.
- If we do that, we're dead.

690
00:46:00,383 --> 00:46:02,135
No, we're playing dead.

691
00:46:02,302 --> 00:46:03,887
And we're making him think
that he's won.

692
00:46:06,848 --> 00:46:07,849
[mic whines]

693
00:46:07,933 --> 00:46:11,686
Cut the power. Cut the engines.
Kill anything that makes a noise.

694
00:46:18,526 --> 00:46:20,111
[power shutting down]

695
00:46:23,239 --> 00:46:24,449
[silence descends]

696
00:46:25,116 --> 00:46:26,493
This better work.

697
00:47:09,786 --> 00:47:10,996
[in sign language]

698
00:47:16,876 --> 00:47:18,169
[moans weakly]

699
00:47:18,253 --> 00:47:20,672
[Ilene] <i>As soon as we move,
he'll be back.</i>

700
00:47:21,297 --> 00:47:23,675
How are we supposed
to get the rest of the way?

701
00:47:30,473 --> 00:47:32,475
How's Kong with heights?

702
00:47:42,986 --> 00:47:44,362
So, what's the plan?

703
00:47:44,529 --> 00:47:47,073
[Bernie] We find out
what's on Sublevel 33.

704
00:47:47,157 --> 00:47:48,324
- [bottle clinks]
- [Josh] Ow.

705
00:47:48,408 --> 00:47:50,076
Keep it moving, tap water.

706
00:47:53,329 --> 00:47:54,497
Go ahead.

707
00:47:58,877 --> 00:48:00,128
[panting]

708
00:48:03,089 --> 00:48:06,092
All right, Mad Hatter.
Down the rabbit hole.

709
00:48:07,552 --> 00:48:09,304
Okay. We got this.

710
00:48:10,055 --> 00:48:11,056
Oh, my God!

711
00:48:11,139 --> 00:48:12,432
[Josh] Are you sure
we can trust this guy?

712
00:48:12,515 --> 00:48:13,516
Yeah, why?

713
00:48:13,600 --> 00:48:15,643
Well, mainly because he says
crazy shit all the time

714
00:48:15,810 --> 00:48:18,605
and carries a bottle of whiskey
from his dead wife like a gun.

715
00:48:19,230 --> 00:48:20,815
I think it's romantic.

716
00:48:20,899 --> 00:48:21,900
Whoo-hoo!

717
00:48:23,151 --> 00:48:25,070
I really don't understand women.

718
00:48:30,825 --> 00:48:31,951
[grunts]

719
00:48:42,504 --> 00:48:43,963
Okay, come on.

720
00:48:47,592 --> 00:48:49,302
- [electricity crackling]
- [gasps]

721
00:48:50,386 --> 00:48:52,972
[Bernie] This whole thing came down,
and there was this...

722
00:48:53,932 --> 00:48:54,933
eye.

723
00:48:56,017 --> 00:48:57,894
[Josh] Uh, what are we looking at?

724
00:48:58,061 --> 00:49:00,396
[Bernie] No, no, no, no.
No, it was here.

725
00:49:00,563 --> 00:49:03,149
I swear to God, it was...
it was right there.

726
00:49:03,274 --> 00:49:04,359
Hey, guys.

727
00:49:05,068 --> 00:49:06,861
- [button beeps]
- [door buzzes]

728
00:49:07,779 --> 00:49:09,739
Anyone know where this leads to?

729
00:49:11,241 --> 00:49:12,242
You believe me, right?

730
00:49:12,325 --> 00:49:13,743
'Cause I know that
there was something here.

731
00:49:13,910 --> 00:49:15,870
[Josh] I'm gonna get a migraine
from that torch.

732
00:49:17,205 --> 00:49:20,375
"Sublevel."
How deep does this thing go, Bernie?

733
00:49:20,542 --> 00:49:22,836
Hell. Goes to hell.

734
00:49:23,920 --> 00:49:25,547
[female automated voice] <i>Sublevel 33.</i>

735
00:49:27,674 --> 00:49:29,175
[male automated voice]
<i>Maglev shuttle departure</i>

736
00:49:29,259 --> 00:49:32,345
<i>to Roswell, New Mexico at 0900 hours.</i>

737
00:49:32,470 --> 00:49:33,805
[mechanical whine]

738
00:49:36,266 --> 00:49:38,059
[Josh] Whoa. [chuckles]

739
00:49:39,269 --> 00:49:40,937
[indistinct PA announcement]

740
00:49:41,521 --> 00:49:42,772
What is all this?

741
00:49:43,273 --> 00:49:45,024
It's breakaway civilization.

742
00:49:45,567 --> 00:49:49,863
I mean, come on. This is page one
in the Apex-playing-God handbook. Huh?

743
00:49:50,029 --> 00:49:53,116
I mean, the Illuminati
running shadow economies

744
00:49:53,199 --> 00:49:55,451
all to fund a hidden colony
for the elite

745
00:49:55,535 --> 00:49:58,371
in case any of these governments
and megacorporations

746
00:49:58,454 --> 00:50:00,582
accidentally hit the doomsday button.

747
00:50:01,875 --> 00:50:04,043
- It makes sense if you think about it.
- Yeah, sure.

748
00:50:04,127 --> 00:50:05,628
[indistinct shouting]

749
00:50:06,754 --> 00:50:07,881
- [Madison] Someone's coming.
- What?

750
00:50:07,964 --> 00:50:08,965
- Someone's coming.
- What?

751
00:50:09,048 --> 00:50:10,717
- [Josh] Someone's coming?
- [Madison] Yes!

752
00:50:15,054 --> 00:50:16,514
Oh, my God.

753
00:50:16,931 --> 00:50:18,308
[muffled squelching]

754
00:50:21,186 --> 00:50:23,897
- [Josh] They look like eggs.
- Skull-crawlers.

755
00:50:24,480 --> 00:50:26,774
What's Apex doing with skull-crawlers?

756
00:50:26,941 --> 00:50:28,234
[man] All right, let's load it up!

757
00:50:28,318 --> 00:50:29,319
- [screams]
- [alarm blares]

758
00:50:29,402 --> 00:50:31,112
[Bernie] What was that?
What was that?

759
00:50:31,196 --> 00:50:33,072
- [engine humming]
- No way. No, no, no. Come on.

760
00:50:33,239 --> 00:50:35,074
Okay, guys, I think we're moving.

761
00:50:52,467 --> 00:50:55,220
It says we're headed
to Apex headquarters in Hong Kong.

762
00:50:55,303 --> 00:50:56,763
- What?
- [Bernie] Hong Kong.

763
00:50:56,930 --> 00:50:59,057
That means that
we're gonna get some answers.

764
00:50:59,224 --> 00:51:01,142
[automated voice] <i>G10, clear for launch.</i>

765
00:51:02,060 --> 00:51:04,062
[engine thrumming]

766
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:10,193
[engine accelerating]

767
00:51:12,028 --> 00:51:13,029
Here we go.

768
00:51:21,746 --> 00:51:23,748
[muffled pulsing]

769
00:51:43,518 --> 00:51:44,811
We're getting close!

770
00:52:09,085 --> 00:52:11,379
- [indistinct radio chatter]
- [alarm blaring]

771
00:52:26,686 --> 00:52:29,480
[harnesses snapping]

772
00:52:47,623 --> 00:52:48,875
[grunts softly]

773
00:52:51,627 --> 00:52:52,879
[moans]

774
00:53:01,304 --> 00:53:02,722
[grunting curiously]

775
00:53:10,396 --> 00:53:11,814
[wind whistling]

776
00:53:18,529 --> 00:53:20,156
[Kong grunting softly]

777
00:53:31,125 --> 00:53:32,210
[in sign language]

778
00:53:35,171 --> 00:53:36,422
[moans]

779
00:53:39,467 --> 00:53:40,551
[snuffles]

780
00:53:46,849 --> 00:53:47,975
[grunts softly]

781
00:53:50,228 --> 00:53:51,270
[snorts]

782
00:53:57,026 --> 00:53:58,403
It's not working.

783
00:53:59,028 --> 00:54:00,738
Just wait. Wait, wait, wait.

784
00:54:00,822 --> 00:54:03,783
What if she tells him
there are others down there like him?

785
00:54:04,826 --> 00:54:05,868
But you don't know that.

786
00:54:06,244 --> 00:54:08,579
We lost our entire fleet getting here.

787
00:54:09,705 --> 00:54:11,207
There's no way back for him.

788
00:54:11,874 --> 00:54:13,751
And he can't survive here.

789
00:54:17,296 --> 00:54:18,381
[growls softly]

790
00:54:22,760 --> 00:54:24,137
[moaning]

791
00:54:27,056 --> 00:54:29,058
All right. All right.

792
00:54:35,982 --> 00:54:37,066
[softly] Hey.

793
00:54:38,609 --> 00:54:39,735
[in sign language]

794
00:54:48,995 --> 00:54:50,121
[sighs]

795
00:55:16,147 --> 00:55:17,398
[grunts softly]

796
00:55:18,274 --> 00:55:19,525
[snarls]

797
00:55:20,985 --> 00:55:24,071
He's going. Prepare to launch!
Everybody to their station.

798
00:55:24,155 --> 00:55:25,156
We gotta go.

799
00:55:36,792 --> 00:55:40,004
[man on PA] <i>All flights crews cleared
for immediate HEAV launch.</i>

800
00:55:40,880 --> 00:55:42,924
[pilot 1 ] <i>HEAV 1 online.
We're clear for launch.</i>

801
00:55:43,257 --> 00:55:45,009
[control] <i>Copy that, HEAV 1.</i>

802
00:55:45,551 --> 00:55:48,012
[pilot 2] <i>HEAV 2 online.
Exiting hangar now.</i>

803
00:55:48,179 --> 00:55:51,307
[control] <i>HEAV 2, confirmation 4055.</i>

804
00:55:51,807 --> 00:55:54,018
[pilot 3] <i>This is HEAV 3 online,
launching now.</i>

805
00:55:54,143 --> 00:55:55,603
<i>We'll follow him from behind.</i>

806
00:56:15,373 --> 00:56:16,415
There.

807
00:56:17,041 --> 00:56:18,251
There he is.

808
00:56:18,334 --> 00:56:19,752
[indistinct radio chatter]

809
00:56:21,504 --> 00:56:22,964
[engine revving]

810
00:56:30,846 --> 00:56:32,056
[growls]

811
00:56:32,139 --> 00:56:34,141
Are you sure the monkey's
gonna survive this?

812
00:56:34,267 --> 00:56:36,644
Oh, he'll be fine.
It's us I'd worry about.

813
00:56:36,811 --> 00:56:39,855
We're about to be launched
1,000 miles in two seconds

814
00:56:40,022 --> 00:56:44,735
until gravity inverts itself
and spits us into free fall.

815
00:56:46,737 --> 00:56:49,031
It'll be the most amazing thing
you've ever seen.

816
00:56:49,115 --> 00:56:50,491
[rumbling]

817
00:56:51,242 --> 00:56:53,077
Here. For the vomit.

818
00:56:53,244 --> 00:56:54,245
What?

819
00:56:57,331 --> 00:56:58,332
[growls]

820
00:57:01,002 --> 00:57:02,295
[Kong groans]

821
00:57:05,798 --> 00:57:07,842
[Maia yelps, panting]

822
00:57:08,634 --> 00:57:09,719
[alarm blaring]

823
00:57:09,844 --> 00:57:11,220
[Kong roaring]

824
00:57:15,099 --> 00:57:16,392
[silence descends]

825
00:57:22,565 --> 00:57:23,816
[grunting]

826
00:57:35,119 --> 00:57:37,288
[distorted screaming]

827
00:57:56,766 --> 00:57:59,977
[automated voice]
<i>Engine failure, gravity low.</i>

828
00:58:00,144 --> 00:58:01,937
<i>- Engine failure.</i>
- [alarm blaring]

829
00:58:02,271 --> 00:58:03,397
[Kong growls]

830
00:58:07,985 --> 00:58:09,487
[alarms blaring]

831
00:58:13,032 --> 00:58:14,450
[screaming]

832
00:58:19,580 --> 00:58:20,956
[Kong groans]

833
00:58:24,168 --> 00:58:25,461
[roars]

834
00:58:34,345 --> 00:58:37,098
All Delta, reverse gravity propulsion!
[screams]

835
00:58:40,768 --> 00:58:42,103
[creatures screeching]

836
00:58:52,196 --> 00:58:54,240
[Maia panting]

837
00:59:20,975 --> 00:59:22,476
[creature squawking]

838
00:59:30,025 --> 00:59:32,194
[creatures chittering]

839
00:59:43,706 --> 00:59:45,207
It's beautiful.

840
00:59:46,000 --> 00:59:47,585
[pilot on radio] <i>This is HEAV 3,</i>

841
00:59:47,668 --> 00:59:49,253
<i>we're getting some
strange radar activity.</i>

842
00:59:49,628 --> 00:59:51,005
<i>We're gonna circle back and...</i>

843
00:59:52,840 --> 00:59:53,841
[gasps]

844
00:59:59,555 --> 01:00:00,681
[creature screeching]

845
01:00:00,765 --> 01:00:02,224
[all screaming]

846
01:00:04,059 --> 01:00:05,352
[Kong growling]

847
01:00:09,315 --> 01:00:10,441
[creature screeching]

848
01:00:14,862 --> 01:00:16,280
[Kong roars]

849
01:00:16,697 --> 01:00:19,241
[roars]

850
01:00:19,742 --> 01:00:20,785
[snarling]

851
01:00:25,873 --> 01:00:27,249
[Kong roars]

852
01:00:28,709 --> 01:00:30,711
All Delta, prepare to attack!

853
01:00:36,675 --> 01:00:38,052
[creature screeching]

854
01:00:38,177 --> 01:00:39,261
[thudding]

855
01:00:43,265 --> 01:00:44,600
[Kong grunting]

856
01:00:47,102 --> 01:00:48,229
[bones crunching]

857
01:00:51,148 --> 01:00:53,484
[creature screeching]

858
01:01:00,199 --> 01:01:01,951
[panting]

859
01:01:04,286 --> 01:01:05,454
[roars]

860
01:01:11,335 --> 01:01:13,295
[grunting]

861
01:01:15,464 --> 01:01:17,258
That's gross.

862
01:01:23,681 --> 01:01:25,850
[Ilene on radio] <i>Kong's on the move.
We gotta go.</i>

863
01:01:31,897 --> 01:01:33,065
[creatures chittering]

864
01:01:38,404 --> 01:01:39,655
[growling]

865
01:01:50,958 --> 01:01:53,294
[Nathan on radio]
<i>Well, he seems to know where he's going.</i>

866
01:01:54,587 --> 01:01:56,755
Oh, he certainly can move.

867
01:02:28,996 --> 01:02:31,165
[thud echoes]

868
01:02:36,045 --> 01:02:37,338
[rocks thudding]

869
01:02:40,257 --> 01:02:41,425
[whines]

870
01:02:48,057 --> 01:02:50,517
[mellow instrumental music playing]

871
01:03:11,622 --> 01:03:12,915
[grunts softly]

872
01:03:15,250 --> 01:03:16,543
[whooshes]

873
01:03:22,549 --> 01:03:24,259
[rumbling]

874
01:03:24,343 --> 01:03:25,970
Okay, okay.

875
01:03:26,345 --> 01:03:28,055
Creepy monorail is slowing down.

876
01:03:28,973 --> 01:03:31,433
[announcer on PA] <i>Attention:
Shipping pod arriving.</i>

877
01:03:31,809 --> 01:03:33,936
[announcer repeating in Cantonese]

878
01:03:34,019 --> 01:03:35,521
[rapid beeping]

879
01:03:37,815 --> 01:03:39,149
[horn blares]

880
01:03:39,233 --> 01:03:40,901
[automated voice speaking indistinctly]

881
01:03:40,985 --> 01:03:43,445
[Bernie] Okay. Keep quiet. Follow me.

882
01:03:44,822 --> 01:03:45,823
[gate thuds]

883
01:03:49,618 --> 01:03:50,619
We're going in?

884
01:03:50,786 --> 01:03:51,954
Yeah.

885
01:03:56,542 --> 01:03:57,543
Oh, no!

886
01:03:59,003 --> 01:04:01,463
Every time, I swear. Doors hate us.

887
01:04:02,339 --> 01:04:04,717
[Bernie] Oh, yeah.

888
01:04:09,888 --> 01:04:11,640
- [Bernie] Aah!
- [Madison] Oh, my God!

889
01:04:12,182 --> 01:04:15,894
It's just so massive. It's so stupid.

890
01:04:16,603 --> 01:04:18,105
So, what is this place?

891
01:04:18,272 --> 01:04:19,982
Well, if there's
a corporate-friendly term

892
01:04:20,065 --> 01:04:21,442
for "sacrifice pit,"

893
01:04:21,608 --> 01:04:23,944
I'd say we are in it.

894
01:04:25,070 --> 01:04:27,156
[Madison] Oh, God, that stinks.

895
01:04:30,242 --> 01:04:32,036
[alarm blaring]

896
01:04:32,786 --> 01:04:34,413
That's not good. Bernie!

897
01:04:34,580 --> 01:04:35,706
[Bernie] I really hate this place.

898
01:04:38,959 --> 01:04:41,003
[automated voice]
<i>Attention: Demonstration</i>

899
01:04:41,086 --> 01:04:43,005
<i>in T-minus one minute.</i>

900
01:04:45,466 --> 01:04:49,053
<i>All personnel
are to stay clear of the area.</i>

901
01:04:49,178 --> 01:04:50,929
[machines powering up]

902
01:04:57,895 --> 01:05:01,106
[engineer] Mr. Simmons,
systems are coming online now.

903
01:05:01,982 --> 01:05:03,275
[exhales]

904
01:05:05,360 --> 01:05:07,362
[metal clanking]

905
01:05:25,881 --> 01:05:27,591
Commence uplink.

906
01:05:27,674 --> 01:05:28,759
[keyboard clacking]

907
01:05:30,427 --> 01:05:31,929
[Ren] Engaging uplink.

908
01:05:32,304 --> 01:05:34,348
[automated voice] <i>Pilot engaged.</i>

909
01:05:36,141 --> 01:05:37,893
[whirring]

910
01:05:41,271 --> 01:05:44,858
[pulsing]

911
01:06:01,125 --> 01:06:03,460
[roars]

912
01:06:04,128 --> 01:06:05,462
[Bernie mumbling]

913
01:06:05,546 --> 01:06:07,464
That's robot Godzilla.

914
01:06:07,631 --> 01:06:09,258
Oh, no. That's...

915
01:06:09,424 --> 01:06:11,135
That's Mechagodzilla.

916
01:06:16,932 --> 01:06:19,059
[metal thudding]

917
01:06:20,269 --> 01:06:22,771
[metal clanking]

918
01:06:30,154 --> 01:06:32,114
[Walter] Release number 10.

919
01:06:32,447 --> 01:06:33,991
[gate thuds]

920
01:06:35,492 --> 01:06:36,660
[snarling]

921
01:06:36,785 --> 01:06:38,537
[both screaming]

922
01:06:39,663 --> 01:06:41,999
[Bernie] Go, go! Go through there!
Madison!

923
01:06:44,835 --> 01:06:46,461
[roars]

924
01:06:46,795 --> 01:06:48,839
[both screaming]

925
01:06:48,922 --> 01:06:50,966
[Bernie] Madison! Run, girl!

926
01:06:51,133 --> 01:06:52,593
Run, girl. Go!

927
01:06:52,676 --> 01:06:54,553
- [skull-crawler roars]
- [Madison shrieks]

928
01:06:56,597 --> 01:06:57,806
[gasps]

929
01:06:59,641 --> 01:07:01,185
[screeching]

930
01:07:09,610 --> 01:07:10,861
[chuckles softly]

931
01:07:18,952 --> 01:07:19,953
[Bernie] Yes!

932
01:07:22,873 --> 01:07:24,458
[system powers down]

933
01:07:28,045 --> 01:07:29,880
- [squelching]
- [Bernie exclaims]

934
01:07:30,297 --> 01:07:31,632
Damn it. [sighs]

935
01:07:32,549 --> 01:07:34,927
[Ren over comms]
<i>System only reached 40% power.</i>

936
01:07:35,093 --> 01:07:36,094
[Walter] Oh, I know.

937
01:07:36,261 --> 01:07:37,554
As expected.

938
01:07:37,721 --> 01:07:40,807
<i>Don't worry. Once the Hollow Earth
sample is uploaded,</i>

939
01:07:40,974 --> 01:07:43,018
our power troubles will be over.

940
01:07:43,185 --> 01:07:45,062
[Ren] If they can find the source.

941
01:07:45,229 --> 01:07:48,899
[Walter] <i>Oh, they'll find it.
I have faith in my daughter.</i>

942
01:07:49,191 --> 01:07:51,401
I have faith in our creation.

943
01:07:51,568 --> 01:07:54,196
And humanity will once again...

944
01:07:54,571 --> 01:07:56,615
be the apex species.

945
01:07:58,116 --> 01:08:01,578
This is why Godzilla attacked
the Apex facility.

946
01:08:02,162 --> 01:08:04,873
[scoffs] They're trying to replace him.

947
01:08:06,333 --> 01:08:08,627
[Mechagodzilla warbling]

948
01:08:17,261 --> 01:08:19,096
[growls]

949
01:08:30,357 --> 01:08:32,109
[Mark] Come on, Maddie.

950
01:08:32,526 --> 01:08:33,652
[signal beeping]

951
01:08:33,735 --> 01:08:36,613
[tech on radio] <i>Sir, Godzilla just made
an abrupt change in direction.</i>

952
01:08:36,697 --> 01:08:37,990
<i>He's moving very fast.</i>

953
01:08:38,073 --> 01:08:40,534
<i>Projections show
he's likely headed to Hong Kong.</i>

954
01:08:40,659 --> 01:08:43,370
<i>Transport is ready
and waiting to take you there, sir.</i>

955
01:08:53,922 --> 01:08:55,632
[thunder cracks]

956
01:08:58,844 --> 01:09:00,220
[mouthing]

957
01:09:04,725 --> 01:09:05,809
[Nathan] That has to be it.

958
01:09:22,117 --> 01:09:26,038
[thunder cracks, rumbles]

959
01:09:28,290 --> 01:09:30,375
[grunts softly]

960
01:09:39,009 --> 01:09:41,470
[growls inquisitively]

961
01:09:47,351 --> 01:09:49,311
[straining]

962
01:10:07,329 --> 01:10:09,581
[energy pulsating]

963
01:10:18,006 --> 01:10:20,425
[roars]

964
01:10:21,093 --> 01:10:24,429
[roar echoes]

965
01:11:01,591 --> 01:11:04,678
[roars]

966
01:11:06,221 --> 01:11:07,889
We were right.

967
01:11:09,015 --> 01:11:10,350
He's home.

968
01:12:34,309 --> 01:12:36,102
[automated voice]
<i>All personnel must display</i>

969
01:12:36,186 --> 01:12:38,396
<i>their Apex employee badge at all times.</i>

970
01:12:39,022 --> 01:12:40,023
[whispering] Follow me.

971
01:12:41,274 --> 01:12:44,819
Lizard people build all their facilities
the same way. I can find the exit.

972
01:12:45,487 --> 01:12:47,072
[Josh gasps]

973
01:12:47,155 --> 01:12:48,698
[Bernie] The exit's this way.

974
01:12:49,199 --> 01:12:51,201
Guys. Madison!

975
01:13:01,086 --> 01:13:02,796
Oh, my God.

976
01:13:05,257 --> 01:13:07,050
[Bernie] Bitch, what?

977
01:13:07,759 --> 01:13:09,261
[Josh] It's a Titan skull.

978
01:13:09,427 --> 01:13:12,013
[Bernie] No, no, no.
That's not just any Titan.

979
01:13:12,597 --> 01:13:14,057
That's Monster Zero.

980
01:13:14,140 --> 01:13:16,393
[gasps] Ghidorah.

981
01:13:21,064 --> 01:13:22,857
[Bernie] They hardwired its DNA.

982
01:13:23,024 --> 01:13:25,026
Self-generating neural pathways

983
01:13:25,110 --> 01:13:27,112
capable of intuitive learning.

984
01:13:27,279 --> 01:13:29,197
[Josh] Okay, I'm smart,
but I only go to high school.

985
01:13:29,364 --> 01:13:31,408
- It's a living supercomputer.
- [Josh] Shh.

986
01:13:33,326 --> 01:13:34,619
[gasps in disbelief]

987
01:13:34,703 --> 01:13:36,371
[Bernie] It had three heads.

988
01:13:37,038 --> 01:13:40,208
Its necks were so long,
they communicated telepathically.

989
01:13:40,625 --> 01:13:43,962
And there's one here
and another one inside of that thing.

990
01:13:44,129 --> 01:13:46,298
Yeah, it could be a psionic interface.

991
01:13:47,173 --> 01:13:48,758
[exclaims] Oh, my God.

992
01:13:50,468 --> 01:13:51,511
[whispers] Careful.

993
01:13:51,803 --> 01:13:52,804
[Madison] It's a pilot.

994
01:13:52,971 --> 01:13:55,640
[Bernie] Yeah. He's in a Trance.

995
01:13:56,266 --> 01:13:58,018
That's a psionic uplink.

996
01:13:59,311 --> 01:14:01,313
It follows his will.

997
01:14:01,896 --> 01:14:04,107
Oh, Apex, what have you done?

998
01:14:16,161 --> 01:14:18,246
[people clamoring and screaming]

999
01:14:19,789 --> 01:14:22,167
[roars]

1000
01:14:25,211 --> 01:14:26,838
- [car alarms blaring]
- [horn blaring]

1001
01:14:27,464 --> 01:14:31,009
[stomping]

1002
01:14:32,093 --> 01:14:34,179
[people screaming]

1003
01:14:34,929 --> 01:14:37,140
[growling]

1004
01:14:47,067 --> 01:14:50,111
This is the day we feared.
I've given the order, Doctor.

1005
01:14:50,278 --> 01:14:51,696
- [people screaming]
<i>- The city is being evacuated.</i>

1006
01:14:53,031 --> 01:14:55,158
[screaming continues]

1007
01:15:00,205 --> 01:15:03,333
[Maia] I don't understand.
He led us here. Where is it?

1008
01:15:05,794 --> 01:15:07,337
[energy pulsates]

1009
01:15:09,297 --> 01:15:10,715
[grunts]

1010
01:15:23,436 --> 01:15:24,604
[Maia] What is he doing?

1011
01:15:50,046 --> 01:15:53,508
[energy surging]

1012
01:15:54,384 --> 01:15:55,844
[Ilene] It's the axe.

1013
01:15:56,052 --> 01:15:59,305
It's drawing radiation from the core
like it's charging.

1014
01:16:25,665 --> 01:16:27,625
[roars]

1015
01:16:33,715 --> 01:16:35,675
[energy charging up]

1016
01:16:41,514 --> 01:16:44,934
[Walter] Whoa! Godzilla's responding!
They found it!

1017
01:16:47,479 --> 01:16:48,813
[siren blaring]

1018
01:16:48,897 --> 01:16:50,440
[Mark] What in the hell?

1019
01:16:59,574 --> 01:17:00,658
[robot chittering]

1020
01:17:04,245 --> 01:17:05,663
What are you doing?

1021
01:17:06,039 --> 01:17:07,749
[Maia] Extracting a sample.

1022
01:17:07,916 --> 01:17:10,001
[Ilene] This is a power
beyond our understanding.

1023
01:17:10,084 --> 01:17:11,544
You can't just drill into it.

1024
01:17:11,711 --> 01:17:13,463
[Maia] Actually, we can.

1025
01:17:16,382 --> 01:17:18,343
My father gets what he wants.

1026
01:17:18,510 --> 01:17:19,844
That's Apex property now.

1027
01:17:20,261 --> 01:17:21,346
[Ilene] What?

1028
01:17:25,934 --> 01:17:27,018
[system beeping]

1029
01:17:27,101 --> 01:17:29,312
Energy signature incoming.

1030
01:17:29,771 --> 01:17:32,565
We should be able to recreate it soon.

1031
01:17:35,693 --> 01:17:37,946
That is the discovery of the millennium.

1032
01:17:38,112 --> 01:17:40,281
- You can't strip it for parts.
- Hold it.

1033
01:17:40,657 --> 01:17:41,825
[guns cocking]

1034
01:17:44,035 --> 01:17:45,078
[roars]

1035
01:17:49,541 --> 01:17:51,000
[rumbling]

1036
01:17:59,384 --> 01:18:01,344
[creatures screeching]

1037
01:18:04,013 --> 01:18:05,098
[Kong growls]

1038
01:18:06,474 --> 01:18:08,142
Go. Go. Got what we needed.

1039
01:18:08,560 --> 01:18:09,686
Let's go!

1040
01:18:10,144 --> 01:18:11,187
[beeping]

1041
01:18:12,230 --> 01:18:13,106
Yes.

1042
01:18:13,231 --> 01:18:16,401
Mr. Serizawa, start your engines!

1043
01:18:16,734 --> 01:18:17,944
The upgrade is untested.

1044
01:18:18,111 --> 01:18:21,197
Once we get online,
<i>Gojira</i> will come straight for us.

1045
01:18:21,322 --> 01:18:25,034
He's been coming for us
since our creation first awoke.

1046
01:18:25,201 --> 01:18:27,495
- We must embrace it.
- We shouldn't rush this.

1047
01:18:27,662 --> 01:18:30,707
We have no idea how this energy source
will affect the Mecha.

1048
01:18:30,874 --> 01:18:32,500
Get in the goddamn chair.

1049
01:18:37,630 --> 01:18:39,007
[Apex guard screaming]

1050
01:18:39,090 --> 01:18:40,508
[Kong growling]

1051
01:18:42,051 --> 01:18:43,052
[gunfire]

1052
01:18:43,136 --> 01:18:44,345
[Apex guard 2 screaming]

1053
01:18:47,932 --> 01:18:49,976
- [Maia] Go, go, go!
- [pilot] Come on, come on!

1054
01:18:50,685 --> 01:18:52,979
Move! What are you waiting for?
Let's go!

1055
01:18:59,652 --> 01:19:02,363
[pilot] This way, sir! Hurry!
We gotta get back...

1056
01:19:02,447 --> 01:19:04,115
- [pilot screams]
- [Ilene exclaims]

1057
01:19:04,240 --> 01:19:06,993
[pilot grunts, screams]

1058
01:19:09,037 --> 01:19:10,413
[creature 2 screeches]

1059
01:19:10,914 --> 01:19:12,624
[creatures snarling]

1060
01:19:13,833 --> 01:19:15,460
[hissing and snarling]

1061
01:19:19,047 --> 01:19:20,381
[squawking]

1062
01:19:22,467 --> 01:19:23,593
[Ilene gasps]

1063
01:19:24,719 --> 01:19:25,720
[screeching]

1064
01:19:28,932 --> 01:19:29,933
Okay.

1065
01:19:30,850 --> 01:19:32,185
- [grunts]
- [screeches]

1066
01:19:32,727 --> 01:19:33,937
[screeching]

1067
01:19:38,024 --> 01:19:39,025
[thuds]

1068
01:19:41,945 --> 01:19:43,029
[Kong grunts]

1069
01:19:55,041 --> 01:19:56,918
[roars]

1070
01:19:59,087 --> 01:20:02,006
[Kong roars]

1071
01:20:06,302 --> 01:20:08,930
Get him out of the way! Shoot him!

1072
01:20:11,349 --> 01:20:12,767
- Go, go, go!
- [roars]

1073
01:20:14,519 --> 01:20:15,520
[thuds]

1074
01:20:17,522 --> 01:20:18,856
[roars]

1075
01:20:19,357 --> 01:20:20,942
- [alarm blaring]
- [Kong growls]

1076
01:20:21,776 --> 01:20:22,860
Oh, no.

1077
01:20:23,653 --> 01:20:24,821
No, no, no...

1078
01:20:27,824 --> 01:20:30,201
[Nathan] Oh, Jesus!
Come on, let's go!

1079
01:20:34,330 --> 01:20:35,498
[thuds]

1080
01:20:37,125 --> 01:20:38,334
[growls]

1081
01:20:49,345 --> 01:20:51,472
[growls angrily]

1082
01:20:57,020 --> 01:20:58,021
[beeping]

1083
01:20:58,938 --> 01:21:00,148
- Hold on, ladies.
- Yeah.

1084
01:21:01,107 --> 01:21:02,108
[Nathan] Whoa.

1085
01:21:23,337 --> 01:21:24,422
[exhales nervously]

1086
01:21:25,423 --> 01:21:26,674
[beeping]

1087
01:21:28,301 --> 01:21:29,677
Stay low.

1088
01:21:31,345 --> 01:21:32,889
[camera clicking]

1089
01:21:33,264 --> 01:21:34,265
[gasps]

1090
01:21:34,682 --> 01:21:36,768
[softly] Yeah. Going viral.

1091
01:21:37,560 --> 01:21:38,561
What?

1092
01:21:39,228 --> 01:21:41,105
We've gotta try and stop this.

1093
01:21:41,606 --> 01:21:43,691
[metal creaking and thudding
in distance]

1094
01:21:44,233 --> 01:21:45,693
I don't like this, guys.

1095
01:21:45,860 --> 01:21:47,695
If this wasn't contributing
to world destruction,

1096
01:21:47,779 --> 01:21:49,155
this would be a great DJ booth.

1097
01:21:53,534 --> 01:21:54,827
I know what it... Maintenance.

1098
01:21:54,994 --> 01:21:56,329
- [Bernie mumbling]
- Madison, we should go.

1099
01:21:56,496 --> 01:21:57,997
[Bernie] I'm Maintenance.
You don't have to alert the...

1100
01:21:58,164 --> 01:21:59,916
She doesn't buy that.
Uh, Madison, we need to go.

1101
01:22:00,083 --> 01:22:01,209
The woman with the villain hairdo,

1102
01:22:01,292 --> 01:22:02,960
- she's getting security.
- Madison, they have guns.

1103
01:22:03,086 --> 01:22:06,214
Hey, guys. Uh, it's soundproof
so I can't really...

1104
01:22:06,380 --> 01:22:08,174
- I wanna communicate...
- Open the door!

1105
01:22:08,341 --> 01:22:09,425
Say again?

1106
01:22:09,592 --> 01:22:11,302
Oh, God! Get down! Get down!

1107
01:22:11,469 --> 01:22:13,304
[Madison] Oh, shit! [gasps]

1108
01:22:18,935 --> 01:22:19,936
[chuckles nervously]

1109
01:22:24,273 --> 01:22:25,525
[car alarm blares]

1110
01:22:25,608 --> 01:22:27,610
[people screaming]

1111
01:22:27,944 --> 01:22:29,612
[Kong growling]

1112
01:22:35,034 --> 01:22:36,369
[roars]

1113
01:22:47,880 --> 01:22:48,881
[growls]

1114
01:22:51,676 --> 01:22:52,718
[growls]

1115
01:22:53,678 --> 01:22:55,429
[both roaring]

1116
01:23:01,811 --> 01:23:03,396
[people screaming]

1117
01:23:04,981 --> 01:23:07,150
- [Godzilla screeches]
- [Kong groans]

1118
01:23:08,234 --> 01:23:09,235
[energy charging up]

1119
01:23:26,460 --> 01:23:27,628
[Kong grunts]

1120
01:23:32,842 --> 01:23:33,885
[roars]

1121
01:23:35,553 --> 01:23:37,054
[energy charging up]

1122
01:24:01,662 --> 01:24:02,872
[roars]

1123
01:24:08,878 --> 01:24:11,130
[Kong growling]

1124
01:24:12,298 --> 01:24:13,424
[sirens wailing]

1125
01:24:25,144 --> 01:24:27,063
[yelping]

1126
01:24:33,236 --> 01:24:34,278
[roars]

1127
01:24:43,246 --> 01:24:44,330
[growls]

1128
01:24:48,459 --> 01:24:50,628
We're about to breach the veil! Hold on!

1129
01:24:55,800 --> 01:24:57,426
[Kong roaring]

1130
01:24:57,510 --> 01:24:58,719
[both screaming]

1131
01:25:14,860 --> 01:25:16,904
- [grunting heavily]
- [exclaims]

1132
01:25:21,117 --> 01:25:22,118
[Kong roars]

1133
01:25:35,506 --> 01:25:36,716
[roars]

1134
01:25:38,509 --> 01:25:39,760
[explosion]

1135
01:25:56,444 --> 01:25:58,571
[grunting]

1136
01:26:01,782 --> 01:26:04,201
Looks like round two goes to Kong.

1137
01:26:04,285 --> 01:26:07,079
[Ilene breathing heavily]

1138
01:26:16,672 --> 01:26:17,673
Hey!

1139
01:26:23,054 --> 01:26:25,848
Oh, come on, guys.
Really? Greenpeace again?

1140
01:26:26,640 --> 01:26:28,642
[laughs] Greenpea...

1141
01:26:28,809 --> 01:26:30,978
Actually, sir,
not like you would know this,

1142
01:26:31,062 --> 01:26:32,855
but I'm Level Two
Assistant Engineering...

1143
01:26:33,022 --> 01:26:35,358
Well, Provisional Level Two
Assistant Engineering,

1144
01:26:35,441 --> 01:26:36,734
not like you would know that.

1145
01:26:36,901 --> 01:26:38,861
My evaluations
were incredibly encourag...

1146
01:26:39,028 --> 01:26:42,990
I'm just saying Greenpeace wishes,
is all I'm saying.

1147
01:26:44,158 --> 01:26:46,744
Where do I know you from?

1148
01:26:49,455 --> 01:26:51,374
Oh, my goodness.

1149
01:26:51,832 --> 01:26:54,627
Director Russell's daughter, yes?

1150
01:26:55,002 --> 01:26:56,629
You caused all of this.

1151
01:26:56,796 --> 01:27:00,966
If by "all of this,"
you mean I, and I alone,

1152
01:27:01,133 --> 01:27:03,552
have given humanity a chance
against the Titans,

1153
01:27:03,719 --> 01:27:06,514
then, yes, I will own that title.

1154
01:27:06,680 --> 01:27:09,016
Godzilla had left us in peace.

1155
01:27:09,183 --> 01:27:10,935
You provoked him into war.

1156
01:27:11,102 --> 01:27:13,771
There can only be one alpha,
Miss Russell.

1157
01:27:13,938 --> 01:27:16,524
It seems to have been providence.
[chuckles]

1158
01:27:35,042 --> 01:27:36,877
[Godzilla growling]

1159
01:27:40,464 --> 01:27:41,674
[Godzilla roars]

1160
01:27:41,841 --> 01:27:42,842
[Kong roars]

1161
01:28:00,526 --> 01:28:01,527
[Kong groans]

1162
01:28:05,948 --> 01:28:07,283
[both growling]

1163
01:28:13,956 --> 01:28:15,249
[groans]

1164
01:28:16,709 --> 01:28:17,960
[Godzilla roars]

1165
01:28:20,546 --> 01:28:21,547
[Kong groans]

1166
01:28:31,015 --> 01:28:32,808
[Kong groaning]

1167
01:28:35,478 --> 01:28:36,479
[groans]

1168
01:28:38,564 --> 01:28:40,524
[Godzilla roars]

1169
01:28:41,692 --> 01:28:43,235
[Kong groaning]

1170
01:28:48,782 --> 01:28:50,075
[growls]

1171
01:29:00,169 --> 01:29:01,587
[Godzilla roars]

1172
01:29:06,759 --> 01:29:08,093
[roars]

1173
01:29:20,105 --> 01:29:21,899
[groans]

1174
01:29:22,483 --> 01:29:23,567
[whimpers]

1175
01:29:38,541 --> 01:29:40,000
[growls weakly]

1176
01:29:40,084 --> 01:29:41,919
[pensive music playing]

1177
01:30:06,652 --> 01:30:10,322
[Walter over comms] <i>It's time to launch.
Begin pilot integration.</i>

1178
01:30:18,289 --> 01:30:19,498
And now...

1179
01:30:20,666 --> 01:30:21,917
my Mecha.

1180
01:30:23,419 --> 01:30:25,629
<i>It's not only Godzilla's equal...</i>

1181
01:30:27,715 --> 01:30:29,466
<i>but his superior.</i>

1182
01:30:29,592 --> 01:30:31,010
[Mechagodzilla powering up]

1183
01:30:31,594 --> 01:30:35,097
The Apex Titan of my own hand.

1184
01:30:35,180 --> 01:30:36,265
[laughs]

1185
01:30:36,807 --> 01:30:39,602
[over comms] <i>It's time to show
the world what you can do.</i>

1186
01:30:42,146 --> 01:30:43,897
[automated voice] <i>Pilot engaged.</i>

1187
01:30:47,943 --> 01:30:51,113
<i>Alert: Failure. System unstable.</i>

1188
01:30:51,280 --> 01:30:55,075
[distorted] <i>Alert: Failure.
System unstable.</i>

1189
01:30:57,411 --> 01:31:00,664
This is how we, as a species, win.

1190
01:31:02,124 --> 01:31:03,584
You see, ten years ago,

1191
01:31:04,126 --> 01:31:07,212
when <i>Gojira</i> was first revealed
to the world,

1192
01:31:07,630 --> 01:31:09,548
I had a dream.

1193
01:31:09,965 --> 01:31:12,885
And in that dream, I saw one thing.

1194
01:31:13,177 --> 01:31:18,682
And that beautiful, amazing thing was...

1195
01:31:21,810 --> 01:31:22,895
Oh, shit.

1196
01:31:23,062 --> 01:31:24,063
No!

1197
01:31:25,522 --> 01:31:26,607
[electricity crackling]

1198
01:31:27,608 --> 01:31:29,276
[grunting]

1199
01:31:32,946 --> 01:31:34,323
[all coughing]

1200
01:31:37,326 --> 01:31:39,244
It's unfair. [coughs]

1201
01:31:39,328 --> 01:31:41,288
I really wanted to hear
the rest of that speech.

1202
01:31:41,580 --> 01:31:42,748
[loud thudding]

1203
01:32:01,850 --> 01:32:03,686
[Mechagodzilla roars]

1204
01:32:06,021 --> 01:32:07,439
[car alarms blaring]

1205
01:32:17,825 --> 01:32:19,243
What in God's name is that?

1206
01:32:29,044 --> 01:32:30,504
[warbling]

1207
01:32:31,296 --> 01:32:33,632
[roars]

1208
01:32:43,058 --> 01:32:44,268
[groans]

1209
01:32:45,102 --> 01:32:46,979
[people clamoring and screaming]

1210
01:32:55,988 --> 01:32:57,364
[metal clanking]

1211
01:33:00,451 --> 01:33:02,161
[groaning]

1212
01:33:04,371 --> 01:33:06,498
It's thinking for itself now.

1213
01:33:06,832 --> 01:33:08,208
We have to warn Monarch.

1214
01:33:09,042 --> 01:33:10,919
Or try to stop it ourselves.

1215
01:33:11,628 --> 01:33:13,172
That thing's still linked
to their satellite.

1216
01:33:13,255 --> 01:33:14,798
[Bernie] Wait, Josh.

1217
01:33:15,466 --> 01:33:19,052
[Josh] If I can figure out the password,
maybe we can shut it down.

1218
01:33:19,219 --> 01:33:20,220
All right.

1219
01:33:28,437 --> 01:33:29,438
[Nathan grunts]

1220
01:33:30,230 --> 01:33:31,231
[Ilene gasps]

1221
01:33:34,193 --> 01:33:35,611
What the hell is that?

1222
01:33:35,778 --> 01:33:37,279
[Godzilla roars]

1223
01:33:55,047 --> 01:33:56,298
[silence descends]

1224
01:34:03,847 --> 01:34:05,599
[muffled heartbeat]

1225
01:34:27,454 --> 01:34:30,499
- What?
- [in sign language]

1226
01:34:34,586 --> 01:34:35,796
What's happening?

1227
01:34:36,672 --> 01:34:38,298
She can feel his heartbeat.

1228
01:34:38,966 --> 01:34:40,008
He's dying.

1229
01:34:40,175 --> 01:34:41,927
[Kong groaning softly]

1230
01:34:42,636 --> 01:34:44,680
There's nothing we can do
to restart his heart.

1231
01:34:44,763 --> 01:34:46,056
We'd need a charge big enough to...

1232
01:34:46,223 --> 01:34:47,891
Light up Las Vegas for a week.

1233
01:35:05,367 --> 01:35:06,368
[roars]

1234
01:35:11,415 --> 01:35:12,624
- [Bernie] Is that a password?
- [system buzzing]

1235
01:35:14,251 --> 01:35:15,419
[shouts] Is that a password?

1236
01:35:15,502 --> 01:35:16,795
I don't know! I'm not used to this.

1237
01:35:16,962 --> 01:35:18,589
I'm used to pirating movies online.

1238
01:35:18,672 --> 01:35:20,007
- Okay, then go to Settings.
- [line ringing]

1239
01:35:20,173 --> 01:35:21,425
- [on phone] <i>This is Mark.</i>
- Dad?

1240
01:35:21,717 --> 01:35:23,594
Madison, where are you?

1241
01:35:23,760 --> 01:35:25,387
<i>Dad, can you hear...</i>

1242
01:35:26,054 --> 01:35:27,723
Can you hear me? I'm in Hong Kong.

1243
01:35:27,890 --> 01:35:29,266
<i>- Mad?</i>
- Dad!

1244
01:35:29,433 --> 01:35:31,268
Mad? Madison!

1245
01:35:31,351 --> 01:35:32,978
[alarm blaring]

1246
01:35:35,981 --> 01:35:37,149
- [engine powers up]
- A-ha!

1247
01:35:37,232 --> 01:35:38,275
[chuckles]

1248
01:35:40,611 --> 01:35:42,529
Okay, you two better get some distance.

1249
01:35:49,161 --> 01:35:50,370
Hey.

1250
01:35:52,331 --> 01:35:54,333
You are a very brave little girl.

1251
01:35:55,500 --> 01:35:56,668
[in sign language]

1252
01:36:02,883 --> 01:36:04,051
I don't know.

1253
01:36:04,384 --> 01:36:05,844
Maybe we both are.

1254
01:36:17,439 --> 01:36:19,900
- [roars]
- [energy charging up]

1255
01:36:20,609 --> 01:36:22,402
[warbling]

1256
01:36:32,955 --> 01:36:35,666
[roars]

1257
01:36:44,633 --> 01:36:45,801
Okay.

1258
01:36:49,805 --> 01:36:51,348
Good luck, big fella.

1259
01:36:52,391 --> 01:36:53,892
[system alarm beeping]

1260
01:36:54,768 --> 01:36:56,395
[beeping intensifies]

1261
01:37:08,115 --> 01:37:09,157
- [explosion]
- [Kong gasps]

1262
01:37:13,286 --> 01:37:14,454
[growls]

1263
01:37:16,665 --> 01:37:18,250
[panting]

1264
01:37:31,596 --> 01:37:32,931
[in sign language]

1265
01:37:35,475 --> 01:37:36,727
[roars]

1266
01:38:06,882 --> 01:38:07,883
[growls]

1267
01:38:18,393 --> 01:38:19,603
[groans]

1268
01:38:21,063 --> 01:38:22,314
[roars]

1269
01:38:24,524 --> 01:38:26,651
- [bones cracking]
- [growls]

1270
01:38:26,777 --> 01:38:28,070
I thought you said you were a hacker!

1271
01:38:28,153 --> 01:38:30,113
I said I took an HTML course
at summer camp.

1272
01:38:30,280 --> 01:38:31,782
- HTML?
- Yes, at summer camp.

1273
01:38:31,948 --> 01:38:34,201
Was it a '90s camp?
Come on. Use QWERTY.

1274
01:38:34,367 --> 01:38:36,536
[automated voice] <i>Error. Security lock.</i>

1275
01:38:36,703 --> 01:38:38,914
- [alarm blaring]
- [Josh] No. Shit!

1276
01:38:39,081 --> 01:38:40,457
Shit.

1277
01:38:41,374 --> 01:38:43,085
[breathing heavily]

1278
01:39:00,769 --> 01:39:01,937
[Godzilla whimpering]

1279
01:39:08,318 --> 01:39:09,820
[Kong roars]

1280
01:39:24,417 --> 01:39:25,502
[Godzilla roars]

1281
01:40:13,675 --> 01:40:14,718
- [whirring]
- [roars]

1282
01:40:18,263 --> 01:40:20,015
[Madison] Josh!
You have to do something.

1283
01:40:20,390 --> 01:40:22,184
We tried to take down
those Apex bastards,

1284
01:40:22,267 --> 01:40:23,393
but I think this is as far as we go,

1285
01:40:23,476 --> 01:40:24,853
so bottom's up.

1286
01:40:25,020 --> 01:40:26,980
I was hoping to die with adults,
but okay.

1287
01:40:32,444 --> 01:40:33,570
[Bernie] If you've never
had a drink before,

1288
01:40:33,653 --> 01:40:34,779
now's the time 'cause...

1289
01:40:35,363 --> 01:40:36,656
Drink. Drink!

1290
01:40:37,115 --> 01:40:38,575
- [Bernie] Hey! What are you...
- [static]

1291
01:40:40,535 --> 01:40:42,037
That's your solution?

1292
01:40:42,120 --> 01:40:44,122
I gotta die here with you, and sober!

1293
01:40:44,247 --> 01:40:45,498
[explosion]

1294
01:40:45,624 --> 01:40:46,750
[whirring stops]

1295
01:40:47,751 --> 01:40:49,544
[electricity crackling]

1296
01:40:53,632 --> 01:40:54,841
[Kong growls]

1297
01:40:57,010 --> 01:40:58,345
[energy surging]

1298
01:41:01,723 --> 01:41:02,766
[grunts]

1299
01:41:05,143 --> 01:41:06,269
